{"reference":"2 Chronicles 28","book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":28,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Israel and Judah","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The account of the captives from Judah treats people from the northern tribes as fellow Israelites: they are called “their brethren,” and the captives are returned to their kin. One reading of Chronicles sees its focus on Judah’s Davidic kings and Jerusalem’s temple alongside an ongoing concern for priests, Levites, worshipers, and captives from the northern tribes as part of all Israel.","verse_refs":["2 Chronicles 28:8-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_chronicles_028_d82ae6b0093fb6b153ad56d5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}